  message: "P4 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 9ae4abe13f; owner-requested re-check of open P4 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p4_review_11012026/graph1/). VERDICT: CURRENT. Review 2026-11-01 at dev 9ae4abe13f. The footer is unchanged at sketch.py:6277 (cited as 6271). Repro: a single-file fixture with 121 functions, hypergumbo sketch -t 2000 --config-extraction heuristic, gives '(... +5 more, top score: 0.00)' followed by '(... and 111 more symbols across 0 other files)'. MECHANISM: The global footer's file-count term counts files with no selected symbol, not the files that hold the unselected candidates."  # 1ef9
- op: discuss  # a55f
  at: '2026-11-14T05:05:56Z'  # a55f
  by: agent  # a55f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a55f
  clock: 3  # a55f
  nonce: a55f  # a55f
  message: "Second outside-reader review, 2026-11-13 (self-run cache f36c63310c791188/results/c872eb7a7e793eab/ac34c56c06ec1788, re-checked on dev fed15705d7, 20 other repositories measured; ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/outside_reader_review2_11142026). SAME SECTION, sibling line. The per-file line '(... +N more, top score: X)' prints the highest centrality among the symbols NOT shown for that file, on a scale that is not normalised: 1.03 under ir.py on the self-run, 2.00 on ripgrep. The line says neither, and it sits under symbols starred as 'centrality >= 50% of max', so a reader took 'top score: 0.09' under a starred find_files for a contradiction. Proposed with this item's fix: label it as the highest hidden symbol and print it on the star's scale (share of the maximum)."  # a55f
